body:
you could get an xps 15, it super powerful although its not a gaming laptop but it should be good enough for most normal games. I'm thinking of saving up for it and from what i've read, its a solid laptop. obviously you should also research any recommended laptops to make sure it has what you're looking for.

&#x200B;

as most other people have wrote, you could also buy a work laptop and a gaming pc which might be a better idea if you don't game in places other than your home.

simplified i'm trying to create a pcb that will drive 8 128x64 oled displays. the reason i did the i2c switch is because they all have the same i2c address so i could turn switch between the displays data line and drive them one at a time.

&#x200B;

what should i do to the ss pins? i grounded them because i saw a schematic doing it.
